(a) whether any channel of official engagement with Pakistan remains active as on date, other than the DGMO-level hotline established after the May 2025 ceasefire understanding;
(b) the details of Government's assessment of, and any advisory issued regarding, the participation of retired Indian diplomats, military officers or civil society figures in Track-2 dialogues with Pakistani counterparts; and
(c) whether the abeyance of the Indus Waters Treaty, declared after the Pahalgam attack, continues and whether any communication has been received from Pakistan on the subject?

(a) whether Government has taken note of 13th DRPSC report of Social Justice & Empowerment Committee observations highlighting underutilisation of funds under schemes such as ADIP, SIPDA, DDRS and scholarships for disabled persons over the last three years, if so, reasons therefor, scheme-wise;
(b) scheme-wise amount allocated, sanctioned, released and utilised for ADIP, SIPDA, DDRS and Scholarship schemes in last five years, year-wise;
(c) whether Government has evaluated impact of factors such as delayed approvals, inter-agency coordination gaps and etc. on implementation of these schemes; and
(d) if so, details thereof, including steps taken to improve utilisation of allocated funds, if not reasons therefor?

(a) the number of road development projects undertaken in the Himalayan States/UTs during the last five years, along with their present status;
(b) whether such projects obtained the necessary Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) and forest clearances and if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether local communities were consulted prior to the commencement of these projects and the manner in which such consultations were conducted;
(d) the number of lanes of roads being constructed under these projects, particularly in ecologically fragile stretches; and
(e) the measures taken by Government to ensure proper disposal of construction debris and waste generated during the execution of such projects?

(a) whether Government is aware that severe heat waves across various parts of the country are leading to widespread sleep loss at night, particularly among vulnerable populations such as elderly, children, outdoor workers and those without access to cooling mechanisms;
(b) whether any studies have been undertaken by Government on health impacts of sleep deprivation caused by extreme nighttime temperatures;
(c) the steps Government has taken/proposed to take to address short and long-term health consequences of disrupted sleep due to rising heat stress; and
(d) whether Government plans to allocate additional resources to State Governments to manage increasing health burden arising from heat-related sleep disturbances?

(a) whether Government has examined the potential food-versus-fuel trade-offs arising from the use of rice, maize, and other food grains for ethanol production, and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether any studies have been conducted on the environmental impact of large-scale ethanol production, including groundwater stress, crop displacement, and emissions balance; and
(c) the roadmap for scaling up 2nd-Generation (2G) ethanol from agricultural residue and non-food biomass, including investment commitments, project timelines, and measures to ensure farmer income gains without increasing food inflation?

(a) whether Government proposes to introduce targeted incentives to accelerate AI adoption among MSMEs, including tax rebates on approved AI tools, AI-linked loans through SIDBI and Mudra and subsidised access to GPUs;
(b) whether Government plans to develop simple, ready-to-use AI toolkits for key MSME sectors such as textiles, retail, logistics and food processing to help them adopt AI more easily;
(c) whether any study has been conducted on the cost barriers faced by MSMEs in adopting AI technologies; and
(d) the timeline by when such incentives or support measures are expected to be rolled out?

(a) the total volume and value of steel imports into the country during each of the last five years, country-wise and category-wise;
(b) the total volume and value of steel exports from the country during the same period, with a break-up PSU-wise (such as SAIL, RINL and other CPSEs) and other domestic producers (private sector), year-wise;
(c) whether Government has analysed the impact of import trends on domestic steel production, capacity utilisation and market share of Indian producers; and
(d) the measures taken or proposed to support domestic steel manufacturers in view of rising imports from specific countries?

(a) the number of sanctioned, filled and vacant posts of coaches and assistant coaches in Sports Authority of India (SAI), National Sports Academies and Regional Sports Schools, year-wise and discipline-wise, during the last five years;
(b) the number of coaches holding international certifications or advanced coaching qualifications, discipline-wise;
(c) the number of athletes currently without access to full-time trained coaches, institution-wise; and
(d) the funds allocated and utilised for coach recruitment, training and upskilling programmes during the last five years, year-wise?

(a) number of children aged 6 months to 3 years, 3 to 6 years, adolescent girls, pregnant, and lactating women, among others enrolled under ICDS, State-wise, year-wise for past five years;
(b) details of beneficiaries receiving supplementary nutrition daily under each category, including weaning food, morning snacks, hot cooked meals, take-home ration, State-wise, year-wise for last five years;
(c) details of immunisation and supplementation provided  including coverage for vaccine-preventable diseases such as poliomyelitis, diphtheria, pertussis, tetanus, tuberculosis and measles, State-wise, year-wise for last five years; and
(d) details of beneficiaries and their outcomes under each ICDS component, State-wise, year-wise for last five years?

(a) whether Government has received reports of delays in payment of incentives, honoraria or other dues to Accredited Social Health Activists (ASHA) workers across States and Union Territories during the last five years and if so, the details thereof, State/UT-wise;
(b) the average duration of delay in such payments during this period;
(c) the reasons cited for these delays, including administrative or fund transfer issues under the National Health Mission (NHM); and
(d) the steps being taken by Government to ensure timely and direct payment to ASHA workers for services rendered?

(a) the number and proportion of Antyodaya Anna Yojana households nationally with more than five members, who would receive less foodgrain under the proposed 7 kg-per-person entitlement capped at 35 kg per household, as against the current flat 35 kg per family;
(b) whether any distributional impact study was conducted before floating the draft Bill, if so the details thereof, if not the reasons therefor; and
(c) the number of public comments received till the 13 July 2026 deadline, and Government's response thereto?

(a) the findings of Government's testing of pre-2023 vehicles running on E20 fuel, referenced by the Union Transport Minister in Parliament on 11th December, 2025;
(b) the current all-India average ethanol blending percentage achieved as against the 20 per cent target and the funds allocated, sanctioned, released and utilised for the Ethanol Blended Petrol Programme during the last three years; and
(c) whether ethanol-free (E0) petrol is mandatorily available at retail outlets, as sought in the pending PIL on vehicle compatibility?

(a) whether Government has proposed the establishment of a new national transport authority to address systemic infrastructure gaps and inefficiencies;
(b) if so, the estimated financial losses incurred during the last five years due to transport-related infrastructure flaws, delays, and coordination failures that necessitate such an authority, year-wise;
(c) details of projects where such losses were incurred;
(d) the proposed functions, mandate, and coordination mechanisms of the authority vis-à-vis existing bodies such as the Ministry of Road Transport & Highways, Railways, and maritime regulators; and
(e) the expected timeline for approval, institutional setup, and operationalisation of this authority?

(a) the States and Union Territories that have formally notified the VB-GRAM-G scheme for implementation as on date, and those yet to do so;
(b) the final Centre-State funding distribution formula notified under the 16th Finance Commission's horizontal devolution principles, State-wise; and
(c) the interim allocation of ?95,692 crore announced for the scheme, and the amount actually released to States, as on date, State-wise?

(a) freight volume carried during each of last five years, commodity-wise and year-wise, including coal, foodgrains, fertilisers, cement, iron ore, steel, petroleum products;
(b) freight earnings realised during the same period, year-wise;
(c) whether Indian Railways has recorded a slowdown or decline in freight traffic or earnings in any of these years, if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether the Ministry has assessed extent to which a modal shift to road transport has affected railway freight volumes, if so, the findings of such assessments; and
(e) the steps taken or proposed to increase freight share, improve logistics efficiency and enhance revenue from freight operations?

(a) the number of human–wildlife conflict incidents reported, during the last five years, State/UT-wise and species-wise;
(b) the number of human casualties, livestock losses and crop-damage cases arising from such incidents, State/UT-wise;
(c) whether Government has assessed the key causes driving the rise in human–wildlife conflict, including habitat loss, fragmentation and linear infrastructure and if so, the details thereof; and 
(d) whether Government has evaluated the effectiveness of mitigation measures, early-warning systems, fencing, relocation efforts and wildlife corridors, including the promptness of compensation disbursal and whether these measures adequately ensure the safety of both people and wildlife and if so, the findings thereof?

(a) the total number of children residing in Child Care Institutions (CCIs) across the country during each of the last five years, State-wise/UT-wise and category-wise, including orphans, abandoned children, and those placed through Child Welfare Committees;
(b) the number of sanctioned, filled and vacant posts of child protection personnel, such as Child Welfare Committee (CWC) members, Juvenile Justice Board (JJB) members, Child Protection Officers, under Mission VATSALYA during the same period, State-wise/UT-wise; and
(c) the number of missing children reported and traced during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise/UT-wise, along with details of the mechanisms used for tracing and rehabilitation?

(a) the total number of toll plazas operational on National Highways during each of the last five years, State-wise/UT-wise;
(b) the total toll revenue collected and expenditure incurred on the running cost of these plazas during the same period, year-wise and State-wise;
(c) the number of toll plazas where user fee collection has been discontinued, State-wise and the reasons therefor; and
(d) whether Government proposes to revise the tolling policy, including rationalisation of user charges and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the estimated demand for major fertilizers during each of the last five cropping seasons;
(b) the corresponding domestic production, imports and total availability of these fertilizers during the same period, year-wise;
(c) the number of States/UTs that reported shortages of any fertilizer during the last five years, along with the quantity of additional stocks reallocated to them; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to ensure timely supply and distribution, including measures for advance stock positioning, import scheduling and real-time monitoring?

(a) the number of reported drone incursions in and around Indian airports during the last five years, airport-wise and year-wise;
(b) the standard operating procedures (SOPs) followed by airport authorities and security agencies when such incursions are detected, and whether any flights were delayed, diverted, or cancelled as a result;
(c) whether any financial losses or operational disruptions were reported due to these incidents, and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures being taken by Government to prevent drone-related security breaches at airports, including deployment of counter-drone systems and coordination with local law-enforcement agencies?

(a) the total value of India’s exports to and imports from all countries with which India has trade agreements, during the five years preceding the implementation of each agreement and during each year thereafter, country-wise;
(b) whether Government has conducted any impact assessments of these trade agreements on India’s merchandise exports, imports, tariff revenue and domestic industry, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the steps taken or proposed by Government to ensure that future trade agreements provide balanced market access, renegotiate unfavourable agreements and adequate safeguards for sensitive sectors of the Indian economy?

(a) estimated crop losses caused by extreme weather events such as heatwaves, unseasonal rainfall, droughts and floods during each of last five years, State/UT-wise, for major agricultural crops including paddy, wheat, pulses, oilseeds, cotton, sugarcane and horticultural produce;
(b) total area affected by such climate-related events during the same period, State/UT-wise;
(c) details of compensation provided to affected farmers under the Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) and other relief mechanisms, State/UT-wise and year-wise; and
(d) whether the Ministry has undertaken any assessment of changing frequency and impact of extreme weather events on agricultural output and farm incomes,if so, findings thereof?

vg

(a) whether Government maintains data on the number of Indian nationals apprehended, detained or deported by foreign countries on grounds of irregular or illegal migration;
(b) if so, the details thereof during the last five years, country-wise and year-wise;
(c) the steps taken by Government, in coordination with State Governments and foreign authorities, to prevent illegal migration and to support affected Indian nationals abroad; and
(d) whether Government has undertaken any public awareness or community-level initiatives to discourage illegal migration and inform citizens about legal migration pathways?

(a) the number of tribal and PVTG villages that have been provided 4G and 5G mobile connectivity during the last five years, along with coverage status, year-wise;
(b) the details of funds allocated, sanctioned, disbursed and utilised therefore including under projects supported through Digital Bharat Nidhi and any initiatives taken under PM–JANMAN for those areas, during the said period, year-wise;
(c) the funds allocated sanctioned, disbursed and utilised for expanding telecom infrastructure in those regions during those years, year-wise; and 
(d) the funds disbursed and utilised  by BSNL and other service providers, year-wise and service provider-wise for providing connectivity in those areas?

(a) whether Government has taken note of the hazardous working conditions faced by workers engaged in waste collection, sewer and septic-tank cleaning, many of whom belong to the Scheduled Castes;
(b) number of injuries and fatalities reported among sanitation and waste-handling workers during the last five years, State-wise/UT-wise;
(c) number of sewer and septic-tank deaths reported during this period and the compensation disbursed in each case, State-wise/UT-wise;
(d) number of sanitation workers who have been provided mechanised cleaning equipment, protective gear, insurance coverage and safety training under central schemes, year-wise; and
(e) number of manual scavengers identified and the number rehabilitated, year-wise and State-wise/UT-wise?

(a) details of the implementation status of the BNS, BNSS, BSA, State-wise;
(b) number of training sessions, workshops or capacity-building programmes conducted for police, judicial officers, other enforcement personnel, cadre/position-wise, State-wise and year-wise;
(c) details of infrastructure, digital systems established or provided to facilitate implementation of these laws, State-wise, year-wise;
(d) whether Government has provided any financial assistance to States for the implementation of these laws, the details thereof, State-wise, year-wise; and
(e) whether Government will ensure that Crime in India report continues to remain comparable with previous years’ data following the adoption of new criminal laws, the measures being taken in this regard?

(a) the details of samples of cough syrups, medicines, oral rehydration salts (ORS), protein powders and other nutritional supplements tested by the CDSCO during the last five years, State/UT-wise;
(b) the number and details of samples found to be substandard or adulterated, along with the action taken against the concerned manufacturers or distributors;
(c) whether Government has launched any special drives to track and prevent counterfeit health and nutritional products and if not, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen drug testing infrastructure and laboratory capacity in States/UTs?

(a) whether Government has conducted any assessment or study on the incidence and causes of fertilizer shortages across various States during the last two years and the details thereof including types of fertilizer;
(b) the impact of such shortages on agricultural output, crop choices, and farmers’ incomes, along with any data collected in this regard;
(c) whether Government has identified structural or supply-chain bottlenecks contributing to recurring shortages; and
(d) the measures proposed or taken by  Government to ensure timely and adequate availability of fertilisers, particularly during peak sowing seasons and abundant monsoons?

(a) whether it is a fact that the IndiGo has expressed willingness to operate flights on the Mumbai–Kalaburagi sector;
(b) if so, the details thereof and the reasons for the delay;
(c) the details of proposals being considered for flights from Kalaburagi to new routes, including Bengaluru, Delhi and Mumbai connectivity; 
(d) the details thereof, including the timeline for starting these services; and 
(e) the details of the status of the proposal for two additional aircraft parking bays, including reasons for delay and expected timeline for approval?

(a) whether it is a fact that the Framework of Roles, Activities and Competencies (FRAC) maps the attitudes, skills and knowledge required for each role performed by a Government employee;
(b) whether Government proposes to assess employees on the basis of such mapped competencies and if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor;
(c) whether Government plans to incorporate competency-based scores for promotion and appraisal processes of Government employees; and
(d) if so, the details thereof, group-wise (Group A, B, C and D) and if not, the reasons therefor?

bs

(a) the number of undertrial prisoners currently lodged in jails across the country who have been awaiting trial or bail for one to two years, two to five years and more than five years, State/UT-wise;
(b) whether aggregate data on pendency of bail applications across courts is maintained through the National Judicial Data Grid (NJDG) or any other mechanism and if so, the details of average time taken for disposal of bail applications, category-wise; and
(c) the measures being undertaken by Government to assist courts in reducing prolonged undertrial detention?

(a) the details of the status of implementation of the Mooshahary Committee recommendations, State-wise and recommendation-wise;
(b) whether Government is considering incorporating Recommendations 42 and 47 of the Committee by amending the Indian Evidence Act, which the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam has replaced and the CrPC which the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita has replaced; and
(c) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total value of pending payments owed to Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) by Central Public Sector Enterprises (CPSEs) and large corporations during the last three years, State-wise and CPSE-sector-wise;
(b) the number of cases recorded on the MSME Samadhaan portal and the number resolved; and
(c) the steps being taken to ensure timely payment compliance and reasons for such delay?

(a) the current status of the remaining construction work under the Central Vista redevelopment project, including timelines for completion;
(b) whether Government is aware of reports of inadequate use of pollution mitigation measures such as dust suppression nets, water sprinklers, or covered transport of debris in and around the Central Vista area;
(c) the measures taken to ensure regular cleaning of roads and removal of construction material that contributes to air pollution in the vicinity; and
(d) whether any environmental audits have been conducted during the ongoing phase of construction, and if so, the key findings and actions taken?

(a) the total revenue earned by Railways from cancellation charges on waitlisted tickets for the last five years, year-wise, travel class-wise i.e., Sleeper Class, 3AC, 2AC, 1AC, Chair Car, etc.;
(b) whether any internal review, audit or public consultation have been conducted on this matter in the last five years; and
(c) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of Tribunals and Appellate Tribunals set up at Sub-Division and District levels under the Maintenance and Welfare of Parents and Senior Citizens Act, State-wise and year-wise during the last five years;
(b) the number of cases brought forward, cases filed, cases disposed and cases pending during the same period, State-wise and year-wise; and
(c) out of the total settled cases, the number of petitioners actually receiving allowances on time as per the orders of the Tribunals, State-wise and year-wise during the last five years?

(a) whether Government has collected or compiled data on inter-State expansion of dairy cooperatives during the last five years, including the number of cooperatives operating in more than one State and the volume of milk procured outside their home States;
(b) State-wise details of procurement volumes, market share and retail presence of such cooperatives;
(c) whether any assessment has been conducted on the impact of such inter-State competition on the financial viability and procurement capacity of district and State-level cooperatives and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen cooperative federalism and safeguard the interests of local farmer-led cooperatives?

(a) total budgetary allocation to Department of Health Research (DHR) as percentage of health budget and as percentage of GDP for last five years;
(b) whether Government has examined concerns raised by 164th Report on Demands for Grants 2025-26 of DHR regarding low allocation, only 3.91 percent of health budget and 0.02 percent of GDP, despite repeated Parliamentary recommendations;
(c) the reasons for non-compliance with Standing Committee’s earlier recommendation that, at least 5 percent of DoH&FW budget and 5 percent of health budget be allocated for health research; and
(d) whether Government proposes to enhance investment in health research over the next five years, as recommended by Committee?

