(a) whether it is a fact that Government proposes to use price data directly from e-commerce platforms for revamping the Consumer Price Index (CPI) and related inflation measures;
(b) if so, the details thereof, including the scope of coverage, cities involved, data-collection timeline and the anticipated changes in weightages for consumption basket;
(c) whether Government plans to discontinue or revise the base years of the existing CPI for Agricultural Labourers (CPI-AL) and CPI for Rural Labourers (CPI-RL);
(d) if so, the details thereof, including the proposed base year and methodology; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government is confident that its current plans for coal exploration, production and usage are consistent with India’s climate goals (including its nationally determined contribution and net-zero by 2070 target);
(b) whether Government has commissioned any recent assessment to evaluate the climate risk posed by planned coal expansion by Government such as an increase in methane emissions; and
(c) the measures being taken to mitigate emissions from coal mines?

(a) whether Indian Railways has issued guidelines to curb the dumping of solid waste from running trains;
(b) the zone-wise number of trains and coaches fitted with functional dustbins and waste-collection mechanisms, in the last five years; and
(c) the year-wise data on solid waste collected from trains and the number of violations detected or penalties imposed for improper waste disposal, zone-wise?

(a) the number of international events hosted in India during the last five years in which foreign teams or athletes withdrew, declined participation or sought rescheduling, year-wise and category-wise, along with specific concerns cited, including air pollution, heat stress, safety or other environmental and health-related factors;
(b) the details of such events, including sports, venues, number of countries originally invited and number of withdrawals;
(c) whether any advisories or contingency measures were issued by sports authorities in response to such concerns; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure that environmental and health-related conditions do not affect athlete safety or international participation in future events?

(a) whether it is a fact that the National Standards for Civil Service Training Institutions (NSCSTI) has been replaced with NSCSTI 2.0;
(b) if so, the reasons therefor;
(c) whether any study has been conducted to assess the implementation of NSCSTI 1.0; 
(d) if so, the details thereof;
(e) the details of ranking of all training institutions accredited under NSCSTI during the last five year, year-wise;
(f) the details of benefits received by institutions with better NSCSTI ratings; and
(g) the details of support provided to lower ranking institutions to improve their ratings, institution-wise and year-wise?

(a) whether it is a fact that training centres were closed during the 2020 and 2021 lockdown, if so, the State-wise details thereof;
(b) whether Government is planning to provide any relief/assistance to such centres, if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and
(c) whether Government is planning to compensate students enrolled in Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY) courses disrupted by the lockdown, if so, the State-wise details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the details of funds allocated, sanctioned and released, sub-scheme wise, for the Modernisation of Police Forces (MPF) during the last five years;
(b) whether it is a fact that the utilisation of allocated budgets by the  State Governments has been low and if so, the reasons therefor; and
(c) whether Government is planning to provide any additional support for infrastructural requirements necessary for the implementation of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita and the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the amount of investment mobilised from private sector entities and multilateral institutions under various initiatives of International Solar Alliance (ISA) since its inception, year-wise and entity-wise;
(b) the number of solar energy projects currently operational under ISA-supported programmes, along with details of their geographical spread across member countries and the details of total megawatt capacity installed, households or beneficiaries reached or other impact indicators;
(c) the details of India’s own participation in ISA-facilitated projects, including projects implemented within india and funds or technical assistance provided; and
(d) whether withdrawal of USA from ISA is expected to affect ISA’s funding, project pipeline or functioning, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of vacant posts in the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI) during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) whether Government has taken note of the 163rd Report on Demands for Grants 2025-26 highlighting that a significant number of vacancies is affecting FSSAI’s regulatory efficiency;
(c) the reasons for the persistent delays in filling these posts; and
(d) the steps being taken to expedite recruitment, reduce dependence on contractual staff and ensure adequate permanent staffing for effective food safety oversight across all States and Union Territories?

(a) estimated reserves of rare earth minerals available in country, mineral-wise and State/UT-wise;
(b) whether Government has assessed projected demand for rare earth elements (REEs) over next 10–15 years, particularly for sectors such as defence, electronics, renewable energy and electric mobility;
(c) if so, details of this assessment and extent to which existing domestic reserves are expected to meet future demand;
(d) whether Government has formulated any policy or strategy for enhancing exploration and processing of rare earths within country; and
(e) steps being taken to reduce import dependence for critical minerals, including collabouration with public sector enterprises, private sector entities or international partners?

(a) whether consultation process was undertaken regarding the total number of days prior to its introduction of draft Viksit Bharat-Guarantee for Rozgar and Ajeevika Mission (Gramin) (VB-G RAM G) Act and its opening for public or stakeholders;
(b) the categories of stakeholders consulted during the drafting process, including State Governments, rural worker organisations, civil society groups, experts, and industry or implementation partners, along with the number of consultation meetings held with each category; and
(c) whether Government has assessed the fiscal implications of the VB-G RAM G Act for States, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of films submitted for certification to the Central Board of Film Certification (CBFC) during the last five years, and the number of films in which the Board directed cuts, modifications, or refused certification;
(b) the category-wise breakup (U, U/A, A, S) of films certified during this period;
(c) the average time taken for certification, including the number of cases where the prescribed timelines were exceeded; and
(d) the number of appeals filed before High Courts against CBFC certification decisions during the said period, along with the number of appeals allowed, modified, or dismissed, year-wise?

(a) whether it is a fact that several AQI monitoring stations in Delhi are situated in low-pollution or residential zones instead of industrial or high-traffic areas;
(b) whether Government has assessed the adequacy and placement of such stations and if so, the details thereof;
(c) if not, the reasons therefor;
(d) the number of AQI monitoring stations upgraded or newly established during the last five years, along with the funds sanctioned, allocated, disbursed and utilised, year-wise; and
(e) the details of plans or proposals for setting up additional AQI monitoring stations in rural and peri-urban areas, along with their current status?

(a) whether Government is aware of the media reports highlighting significant discrepancies between the Air Quality Index (AQI) figures reported by the Central Pollution Control Board (CPCB) and international sources such as IQAir;
(b) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; and
(c) the steps being taken to ensure greater transparency, accuracy and international comparability of India’s AQI data?

(a) number of One-Stop Centres (OSCs) currently operational in the country, States-wise/UT-wise;
(b) number of sanctioned posts and actual staff in each OSC;
(c) whether all OSCs have access to trained counsellors, legal aid support, medical assistance and temporary shelter facilities as mandated under the scheme;
(d) number of women who have availed services at OSCs during last five years, including a break-up of services such as counselling, legal support, medical assistance and emergency shelter; and
(e) whether any gap has been identified in the functioning of OSCs, including delays in funding, staff shortages or lack of coordination with police, legal services authorities or district administrations?

(a) the progress made towards achieving key National Education Policy (NEP), 2020 targets, including, increasing Higher Education GER to 50 per cent by 2035, achieving 100 per cent school GER by 2030, Universal Foundational Literacy and Numeracy (FLN) by 2025, 100 per cent ECCE coverage by 2030, and providing vocational exposure to 50 per cent of learners by 2025; 
(b) whether Government has assessed the reasons for delays in meeting targets, and if so, the details thereof; 
(c) the steps being taken to accelerate progress on these NEP goals, particularly in States that are lagging behind; and 
(d) whether Government proposes revising timelines for NEP targets in view of recent data indicating slow progress?

(a) the number of National Tele Mental Health Programme (NTMHP) cells sanctioned, operational and functional during the last five years, State-wise and year-wise;
(b) the details of personnel sanctioned, in position and vacant for these cells, cell-wise, State-wise and year-wise;
(c) the number of calls received, attended and resolved by these cells, cell-wise, State-wise and year-wise; and
(d) whether these cells are mandated to conduct periodic follow-up or check-ups on callers and if so, the details thereof?

(a) details of the number of applicants, registered beneficiaries, beneficiaries provided basic skill training, beneficiaries certified, beneficiaries provided concessional loans and supplied modern tool-kits, since inception of PM Vishwakarma Scheme's skill-wise, State-wise and year-wise ;
(b) whether any placement support was provided to beneficiaries, if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; 
(c) details of budget sanctioned, allocated, released and utilised, since its inception year-wise; and
(d) whether any support for brand promotion and market linkages has been established to help Vishwakarmas access new opportunities for growth and if so, the details thereof?

(a) number of road projects sanctioned, and total length of roads constructed in tribal-dominated areas under various schemes, including  Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY), during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) status of incomplete or ongoing road works in tribal regions, including reasons for delays, if any;
(c) whether the Ministry has assessed quality and durability of such roads, particularly their ability to withstand monsoons, hilly terrain, and other challenging local conditions; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and whether any steps have been taken to improve design standards, maintenance, or all-weather resilience of roads in tribal areas?

(a) whether it is a fact that several Government websites have obtained Certified Quality Website (CQW) status, if so, the details thereof, including the names of certified websites, issuing authority, date of issuance and date of expiry of each certificate;
(b) the number of Ministries and Departments that have applied for CQW certification and the number of applications requested, processed, approved, rejected and pending, Ministry-wise and year-wise; and
(c) whether Government proposes to expand, revise or mandate CQW certification across all Government websites, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of RTI applications received by each Ministry/Department of Government during the last five years;
(b) the number and percentage of RTI applications rejected by each Ministry/Department during this period;
(c) the reasons most frequently cited for such rejections, Ministry/Department-wise; and
